From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:02:00 -0400
Subject: fix: deleting the active Space, collapsing its folder, and little
 windows

Deleting the active Space switches to the next Space, or the previous one
if it was last, and then moves the tabs there. Only the last Space stays.
Another window that was showing the deleted Space lands on that same
neighbour.

Collapsing a folder keeps the active tab under the header and does not
switch tabs. The visibility pass uses the same rule, so a later Space
change does not bring the hidden rows back.

Badge 9 is the last visible row, which is the row Command-9 selects.
A little window no longer offers Space commands: Control-1 through 9 do
nothing there, and the command bar has one row, Open in main window.

Why: those four behaviours are what the owner decided, and the previous
patch left each of them as it was.
Removable when: Spaces, folders and little windows are withdrawn.
